<title>DUBAI: Saudi Aramco raises Gulf bunker prices.</title>
<headline>Saudi Aramco raises Gulf bunker prices.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Aramco said on Wednesday it had increased A-960 bunker prices from Ras Tanura and Dammam by $2 a tonne to $121 a tonne ($18.57 a barrel).</p>
<p>A-960 from the Red Sea ports of Jeddah and Yanbu was left unchanged at $120 a tonne ($18.42).</p>
<p>A-888 bunker diesel prices are $5 a tonne higher from all four ports at $209 a tonne.</p>
<p>The prices go into effect September 19.</p>
<p>-- Dubai Newsroom, +971 4 6071255</p>
</text>
